title The flag that said two things -- door B lands, eight rows take BOOKED, and the pin drains 24,828 to 5,388
prompt Keaton's kg with all recommended doors granted; N=3750 turned the rota to aether's second orbit turn, and the pin-deadlock design named its own recommended door -- B, the one that reaches the cause.
think The aether application: a guard that cannot red guards nothing, and a guard nobody runs guards nothing either -- so slice one seated the fn-drift witness on construction/standing-equipment.kyri at the lap tier, committed and pushed in one breath because a fresh loop (grain-16, the relaunched Silence most likely) works this same checkout and round-opens stash whatever lingers.
think Door B, the mechanism: the fold script tools/fixtures/r/reds_fold.sh now reads a row's LAST bold status marker first -- BOOKED and CLOSED fold, OPEN refuses, markerless keeps the elder whole-word test -- and the same case moved into the shared reader tools/fixtures/r/reds_pin_capacity_rows.awk (fold_refused calls last_marker) and into reds_status_consistency_scan.sh, whose fold_blocked reading narrows to markerless rows and which prints booked_rows. The control plants both directions (a BOOKED row with the bare word OPEN folds and leaves the pin; a bold-OPEN row refuses by name), 27 of 27. The vocabulary seats in reds-first.md and its .cursor twin with one identical bullet, and in the pin's own Key header: three status words, the last marker decides, read one way everywhere.
think The honest re-reading the door demands: eight pin rows took BOOKED with their remainder kinds named -- %291 (a seat: one tree per star or a lock, with all agent-doable habits adopted), %301 (five booked folds), %306 %326 %327 %328 (seats), %311 (a ratchet), %330 (the rename lap). The pin wall itself forced the timing: the Key addition pushed the page 252 over, and the drain WAS the trim. The fold moved all eight to construction/archive/REDS-the-booked-remainders-rows-291-330.md -- the first fold the tool accepted under the new word -- and the pin fell 24,828 to 5,388 bytes against its 24,576 bound. The ledger can book reds again with nineteen kilobytes of breath.
obs Two refusals inside the lap, both kept: an apostrophe in a comment split the shell's single-quoted awk program (the consistency scan died at "defect's" -- reworded, the oldest quoting trap); and the fold witness refused pass=23 against a control grown to 27, updated with the four door-B behaviors named in the assert message. The capacity witness's agreement check then proved pin 0 plus shelf 2 equals spine 2 -- exactly %337 and %338, the two live reds still exiled on shelves.
obs Doors that opened by closing this one: %337 and %338 could now COME HOME to the drained pin (the pin keeps what is open, and it finally has room) -- a careful accretion question for its own lap; and %338 itself can take CLOSED once a closure note's grammar is read properly, since door B was its repair. Named, not rushed.
